  body: "# Change of circumstances and assessed income periods\n\n**Model-assisted source interpretation;
    unreviewed. No entitlement decision or executable rule.**\n\nThe captured payment guidance says a
    change of circumstances can provide grounds for supersession and directs readers to the AIP chapter
    for changes during an assessed income period.\n\n## Evidence and scope\n\n[DMG 79050, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e1035298c6c9802f7ed9e0/dmg-Chap-79.pdf#page=6)
    supports this scoped proposal. The source PDF SHA-256 is `0098a2267cb9b321cae6bf25b3493b3674c4e8cb1b859fcd6b8ae7d459323be8`.\n\
    \nA change does not itself prove a new award outcome. The AIP's historical boundary and decision-making
    legislation must be checked.\n\nThe capture date, the publication page's update date and a date stated
    in the guidance have different meanings. Linked legislation and memos need their own provision, version
    and applicability review.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/assessed-income-period
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source makes an explicit cross-reference from changes of circumstances to AIP
      guidance, which prevents a blanket change rule being inferred.
    evidence:
    - page: page/79/0006
      quote: "79050 A change in the claimant’s circumstances can give grounds to supersede the award 1.
        But see\nDMG Chapter 83 regarding changes during the AIP.\n\n\n                              \
        \                                                   1 SS Act 98, s 9 & 10"
